add('Labels: validation masks only, read by `score.py` and `verify.py`. ROC-AUC, AP, base rates, conditional precision/recall, same-label rates, matched-recall envelopes and majority-precision boundaries use these labels. Affinity thresholds, overall attraction rates, patient/image counts, feature checks and runtimes do not use segmentation labels. Extraction and affinity generation install an explicit annotation-read prohibition; all scripts prohibit writes outside this investigation. Training-label reads are forbidden.')
add('### Exact reuse and sampling')
add('`extract.py` imports the actual `LitUnsupervisedSegmenter`, dataset preprocessing and image-only loader. It calls `BiomedCLIPFeaturizer.forward` (`src/modules.py:200`), instrumenting its actual trunk call to capture normalized blocks 9, 11 and 12, with CLS excluded. Its final output is retained and verified. Blocks are one-based, final=12. The source checkpoint supplies the unchanged frozen backbone, not learned affinity scores.')
add('`affinities.py` AST-imports CROSSPATIENT `batches`/`image_id_codes` and PAIRS `spy_sample`/`hard_labels`; calls the actual `ContrastiveCorrelationLoss.forward` and `helper` (`src/modules.py:473`, `src/modules.py:499`). Positive scalar ID codes have cosine one and expose affinity by inverting the helper return. No affinity or restored-mean equation is reimplemented. Uncentered variants call that same helper with a diagnostic config copy having `pointwise=False`. Project configs remain unchanged.')
add(f'Seed {meta["seed"]}. Seven deterministic shuffled passes through all slices, batches 16 (last 8), actual 11×11 sampled coordinates. The current config uses the top seven non-self neighbours; the actual dataset loader verified the cache identity, order and values. Every cached top-seven edge is used once. Random pairs retain the first actual nonzero roll per batch, including both same-patient and cross-patient images. This is the actual negative-image sampler, not exclusively cross-patient sampling. There are {meta["rows_per_pool"]:,} image-pair draws and {meta["pairs_per_image_edge"]:,} label-free uniformly selected entries from each 121×121 matrix: {meta["pairs_per_pool"]:,} scored pairs per pool. All variants share identical image pairs, coordinates and retained pair indices. These are Monte Carlo pair estimates across the full cohort, not exhaustive enumeration of all possible pairs.')
add('Loss centering is performed on the FULL actual batch correlation tensor before retaining sampled entries. Final/block features are LayerNorm-normalized trunk outputs; the actual helper applies channel L2 normalization after spatial sampling. The train-mean alternative subtracts the all-training raw-token mean, L2 normalizes each grid token, then uses the actual sampler and helper. Its primary result has no restored-row centering; the additional “+ loss centering” variant is reported separately. All features are evaluated with dropout off; source variants retain the SAME final-feature cache neighbours.')
add('The K8 reference is `audit/scratch/baseline/k8_c0_s0_assignments.npy`, produced previously by `baseline/kmeans.py --k 8 --center 0 --seed 0` on all training slices without fit labels. No validation-derived cluster-to-organ mapping is used here: affinity is simply whether the two sampled nearest tokens share a cluster. It has only one nontrivial operating point. Continuous features are bilinearly sampled; discrete annotations/cluster membership follow PAIRS nearest sampling.')
